diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index e4d1c1a..bd8d858 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -17,6 +17,18 @@ index. It is shown in a read-only field on `/bots` and is the credential used
 by the posting API; bots don't have passwords (the `password_digest` column is
 nullable now so direct SQL/fixture inserts don't need one).
 
+## Limits
+
+Administrators can cap how many bots each member may own from **Account settings**
+(`/account/edit`) using the **Bots per member** number field, which defaults to 5.
+Administrators aren't limited, and only live bots count: deleting a bot frees up a
+slot, while lowering the limit never removes existing bots—it only blocks new ones.
+
+A member at the limit sees a "You've reached the limit…" note on `/bots` instead of
+the **Add a chat bot** button, and `BotsController` refuses both `GET /bots/new` and
+`POST /bots` with `403 Forbidden`. `Bot` also validates the limit on create, so bot
+creation is refused no matter the entry point.
+
